  "id": "occasionalism",
  "term": "occasionalism",
  "definition": "Occasionalism is the historical doctrine that mind and matter do not directly cause changes in each other; instead, when one changes, God produces the corresponding change in the other. In this view, each side is only the occasion for divine action rather than a true efficient cause of the other.",
